    "methods_description": "Each trial had a jittered fixation interval (600-1000 ms), a first memory screen (1000 ms) with cued lateral objects that were studied or novel, a 1400 ms interval, and a second screen (1000 ms) of vertical novel items appearing on 80% or 20% of trials depending on the load expectation condition. After a 400 ms interval, a probe from either screen was shown and participants reported its color via mouse on a continuous color wheel, followed by angular error feedback and corrective feedback for studied objects with errors over 40°.",
